The problem was in the trigger: `fflib_SObjectDomain.triggerHandler` must be given the domain's `Constructor` class (which implements `IConstructable`), not the domain class itself. With `Opportunities.class` passed in, the framework could not construct the domain object, so `onValidate`/`onValidate(Map<Id,SObject>)` were never invoked and no errors were ever added — explaining why all three tests observed a successful save instead of a failure.

